{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779166257,"nonce":"6BBJzBeU6VIiiiNdLIyZDyEjNlM=","message":"## Reframed priority after Scenario Projection Workspace merge\n\nThis issue is now the direct follow-up to the merged objective/scenario authoring work in `0d82869`.\n\nThe current UI has enough selector plumbing to expose the gap: graph ports can be selected, objective source/target paths can be edited, and there is a quick substate/path field. That is not yet a real state browser. Users still need to inspect and select structured internals such as `mechanics.effector.position`, final velocity, indexed arrays, slices, hidden states, task fields, artifact fields, and analysis outputs with enough metadata to know whether a selector is valid.\n\nUpdated expected shape:\n\n- Backend/runtime introspection should enumerate reachable state/object trees for the active scenario/model/task/mechanics context, including path, kind, shape, dtype, units/frame when available, and compatibility hints.\n- The UI should provide a searchable tree/list browser that can be opened from objective source/target fields, probe/metric authoring, and graph/workspace inspector actions.\n- Selection should create or update the same typed selector records used by `Graph / Workspace / Objectives`; compact path strings can remain as serialization, but should not be the only UI model.\n- Array/tensor fields need affordances for indices, slices, final/sample/window selectors, and event/phase-relative temporal selection where the field is time-varying.\n- Imported or synthetic examples such as RLRMP should label missing introspection data honestly instead of implying full authored scenario metadata exists.\n\nThis should land before task-aware metric columns (`e5a1e6c`) because metric specs need the same selector/state introspection substrate.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}